<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raya Malla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raya Malla was the first king of the separate kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhaktapur">Bhaktapur</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu-valley">Kathmandu Valley</a>. When his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaksha-malla">Yaksha Malla</a> died in 1482, the Malla realm was divided among his sons: Raya Malla kept Bhaktapur, the old capital in the east of the valley, while his brothers founded Kantipur and other seats, beginning the rivalry of the valley kingdoms.</p></div>
